[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1119,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 1158,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154368,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 9,
        "headingId": 1158,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Myolipoma of soft tissue is a benign extrauterine neoplasm composed of mature adipose tissue and well-differentiated smooth muscle cells.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:34:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1120,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 1159,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154369,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 9,
        "headingId": 1159,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8890/0 Myolipoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:34:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1121,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 1160,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154370,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 9,
        "headingId": 1160,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2E80.01 &amp; XH4VB4 Deep subfascial lipoma &amp; Angiomyolipoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:34:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1122,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 1161,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154371,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 9,
        "headingId": 1161,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> extrauterine lipoleiomyoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:34:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1123,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 1162,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154372,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 9,
        "headingId": 1162,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:34:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1124,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 1163,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154373,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 9,
        "headingId": 1163,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Myolipoma usually presents as a deeply situated mass within the retroperitoneum, abdominal cavity, pelvic cavity, or inguinal region. Less commonly it occurs in the trunk wall, the pleura, or the extremities; even an intraosseous lesion has been reported {27635945; 1703396; 7959650; 34584729; 38508597}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:34:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1125,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 1164,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154374,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 9,
        "headingId": 1164,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Lesions within the abdominal cavity are often found incidentally, whereas those involving the trunk or extremities present as palpable lesions {27635945; 1703396}. MRI shows a fatty mass with associated signal-rich areas (corresponding to the smooth muscle component) that are heterogeneous on T1-weighted postcontrast fat-suppressed images {17325918}. Hormone-secreting neoplasms may occur {38362362}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:34:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1126,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 1165,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154375,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 9,
        "headingId": 1165,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Myolipoma is a rare tumour occurring chiefly in women. It is not associated with tuberous sclerosis {27635945; 1703396; 7959650}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:34:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1127,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 1166,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154376,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 9,
        "headingId": 1166,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:34:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1128,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 1167,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154377,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 9,
        "headingId": 1167,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Cytogenetic alterations of the <em>HMGA2</em> gene have been reported {26857357; 12419585}. Fusion of the <em>HMGA2</em> and <em>C9orf92</em> genes resulting from a t(9;12)(p22;q14) was noted in 1&nbsp;case of myolipoma {26857357}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:34:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1135,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 1174,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154378,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 9,
        "headingId": 1174,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Deep myolipomas are frequently large, often reaching 100&ndash;250&nbsp;mm in size. Giant neoplasms may mimic a more aggressive neoplasm {38524654}. Superficial lesions are smaller. The tumour is well circumscribed and usually surrounded by a thin capsule. The cut surface shows an admixture of yellowish adipose tissue and tan-whitish whorled nodules, depending on the amount and distribution of the smooth muscle component {27635945; 1703396; 7959650}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:34:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1129,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 1168,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154379,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 9,
        "headingId": 1168,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The lesions are composed of an intimate admixture of mature fat cells and spindled cells, in variable proportions. The spindled areas consist of well-differentiated smooth muscle, with intersecting fascicles of amitotic, cytologically bland cells having eosinophilic cytoplasm, cigar-shaped nuclei, and occasionally perinuclear vacuoles. The adipocytic component lacks any features to suggest atypical lipomatous tumour&nbsp;/ well-differentiated liposarcoma (e.g. enlarged cells with enlarged and atypical nuclei, fibrous septation, lipoblasts) {27635945; 1703396; 7959650}. The lesions usually contain variable numbers of small blood vessels and uterine-type thick-walled vessels {27635945}. Immunohistochemically, desmin, caldesmon, and SMA positivity confirms smooth muscle differentiation. Nuclear positivity for HMGA2 is identified in 60% of cases. ER and PR are often positive. MDM2, CDK4, and HMB45 are negative {27635945; 1703396; 8872156; 25517956; 15144408}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:34:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1130,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 1169,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154380,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 9,
        "headingId": 1169,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Insufficient data</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:34:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1131,
